A data analyst in IT collects, cleans, transforms, and visualizes raw data to help companies make smart choices.
Key Responsibilities
• Data Gathering: Extract information from databases and spreadsheets using SQL and APIs.
• Data Cleaning: Fix errors, remove duplicates, and format raw files so they are ready to study.
• Data Analysis: Run statistical checks to find trends, patterns, and answers to business problems.
• Visualization: Build clear charts, graphs, and interactive dashboards using tools like Power BI or Tableau.
Essential Tools
• Querying: SQL, PostgreSQL, or MySQL.
• Spreadsheets: Microsoft Excel and Google Sheets.
• Visualization: Tableau and Power BI.
• Programming: Python or R for advanced data work.
